e + 1 dispatch, bit-identical.\n- Silent tier-loss class (3 found): any LLVM verifier failure silently drops the WHOLE program\n  to Cranelift. Fixed instances: CallIndirect int widths (17bdedc2), float\u003c-\u003eint backstop\n  (c33c25ab). ROOT compiler bug still open: Int locals decay to Float in MIR under the\n  if-reassign-min shape (stealLoop needed explicit :Int annotations).\n- **Adding methods to a cross-module-used class (SpinPool) breaks importers' dispatch of OTHER\n  methods** (member-layout drift, bugs_import_xmodule_member_resolution): LlamaModel.shutdownPool's\n  spinPool.shutdown()/profReport() mis-dispatch → workers are currently ABANDONED at exit (not\n  joined) and the pool profile must be printed from INSIDE SpinPool (periodic report every 512\n  dispatches in parallelRows). This disease keeps eating instrumentation — fix the general\n  x-module member resolution or stop touching SpinPool's member list.\n- Segfault post-mortems this session: (1) batch\u003e1 Mem-scratch accumulator corrupted heap\n  (f32-pattern fault addresses) — reverted, root not fully diagnosed (suspect closure-capture\n  interaction); (2) stealLoop Float-decay verifier fail → cranelift fallback → downstream crash.\n- rayzor.Mem intrinsics (loadF32/storeF32/loadF64/storeF64/loadU8/storeU8/loadI32/storeI32/\n  f32FromBits) = address-based single-MIR-instruction accessors (1cebd839, 5e4e5b8c) — THE tool\n  for kernel work; Bytes.loadI32AlignedUnchecked pair = handle-based equivalents.\n- Prefill: batch-inner + stealing → prefill_fwd ≈ 40ms/token (better than decode/token now).\n- --tier-promotion false CLI flag with llama-chat's manifest routes main through the interpreter\n  and breaks — use the [tier] block to change promotion, not the flag.\n\n- THE reliable benchmark is llama-chat-server bench_server.sh (worker-style, cooldowns, stddev\n  \u003c2), NOT standalone `run` (heat-soaks + drifts 64-80 unreliably). User's serving flags:\n  RAYZOR_HAXE_MATMUL=1 RAYZOR_WORKERS=1 R